+(duration-type)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a
+{class}`~datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole number of seconds,
+like `120`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units `d`, `h`,
+`m`, and `s`, like `2d`, `1h30m`, or `1d2h3m4s`. Each unit may appear at
+most once and in that order, with no spaces. Units are case-insensitive, so
+`45S` is accepted too.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=30m1h'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
+```{versionadded} 8.6.0
+```
+
